        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:royal-commissions-amendment-act-2013-sch-1-sec-6oc-ss-4-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "applies",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Applies section 9 to records",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(4) Section 9 (custody and use of records of Royal Commission)",
      "cml:conclusionText": "also applies as if a record produced by one or 2 members of the Child Sexual Abuse Royal Commission at a private session were produced by the Commission."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:royal-commissions-amendment-act-2013-sch-1-sec-6oc-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "6OC(5) Status of private session",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/royal-commissions-amendment-act-2013#sch-1-sec-6oc-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "royal-commissions-amendment-act-2013.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "royal-commissions-amendment-act-2013.pdf, p.13",
      "values:originalText": "(5) Sections 6H (false or misleading evidence), 6I (bribery of witness),\n6J (fraud on witness), 6L (preventing witness from attending), 6M\n(injury to witness) and 6N (dismissal by employers of witness)\napply as if:\n\n(a) a person who appears, or intends to appear, at a private\nsession were called or summoned, or appeared, as a witness\nbefore the Child Sexual Abuse Royal Commission; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2013A00024\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments\n\n(b) any information provided, or that a person intends to provide,\nat a private session were testimony or evidence given at a\nhearing before the Commission; and\n\n(c) any document or other thing that a person produces, or\nintends to produce, at a private session was produced or\nwould have been produced because the person was required\nto do so under a summons, requirement or notice under\nsection 2.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) Sections 6H (false or misleading evidence), 6I (bribery of witness),\n6J (fraud on witness), 6L (preventing witness from attending), 6M\n(injury to witness) and 6N (dismissal by employers of witness)\napply as if:\n\n(a) a person who appears, or intends to appear, at a private\nsession were called or summoned, or appeared, as a witness\nbefore the Child Sexual Abuse Royal Commission; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2013A00024\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments\n\n(b) any information provided, or that a person intends to provide,\nat a private session were testimony or evidence given at a\nhearing before the Commission; and\n\n(c) any document or other thing that a person produces, or\nintends to produce, at a private session was produced or\nwould have been produced because the person was required\nto do so under a summons, requirement or notice under\nsection 2.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:royal-commissions-amendment-act-2013-sch-1-sec-6oc"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:royal-commissions-amendment-act-2013-sch-1-sec-6oc-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:royal-commissions-amendment-act-2013-sch-1-sec-6oc-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:royal-commissions-amendment-act-2013-sch-1-sec-6oc-ss-5-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:royal-commissions-amendment-act-2013-sch-1-sec-6oc-ss-5-logic-argumentation-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:royal-commissions-amendment-act-2013-sch-1-sec-6oc-ss-5-logic-diffusion-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:royal-commissions-amendment-act-2013-sch-1-sec-6oc-ss-5-logic-cogai-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "0ec0ddb13de9edbbab85b5bf03cf9c64de62174b8af9bbf7a15a423d6e03e6f3",
      "skos:note": "Sections 6H-6N apply as if a person appeared at a private session before the Child Sexual Abuse Royal Commission."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/royal-commissions-amendment-act-2013#sch-1-sec-6oc-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6OC(5) Status of private session",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 13,
      "values:originalText": "(5) Sections 6H (false or misleading evidence), 6I (bribery of witness),\n6J (fraud on witness), 6L (preventing witness from attending), 6M\n(injury to witness) and 6N (dismissal by employers of witness)\napply as if:\n\n(a) a person who appears, or intends to appear, at a private\nsession were called or summoned, or appeared, as a witness\nbefore the Child Sexual Abuse Royal Commission; and\nComLaw Authoritative Act C2013A00024\n\nSchedule 1  Amendments\n\n(b) any information provided, or that a person intends to provide,\nat a private session were testimony or evidence given at a\nhearing before the Commission; and\n\n(c) any document or other thing that a person produces, or\nintends to produce, at a private session was produced or\nwould have been produced because the person was required\nto do so under a summons, requirement or notice under\nsection 2."
    },
