      },
      "dc:source": "royal-commissions-amendment-act-2013.pdf, p.14",
      "values:originalText": "session are not admissible in evidence\n\n(1) The following are not admissible in evidence against a natural\nperson in any civil or criminal proceedings in any court of the\nCommonwealth, of a State or of a Territory:\n\n(a) a statement or disclosure made by the person at a private\nsession;\n\n(b) the production of a document or other thing by the person at\na private session.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply to the admissibility of evidence in\nproceedings for an offence against this Act.",
      "skos:definition": "session are not admissible in evidence\n\n(1) The following are not admissible in evidence against a natural\nperson in any civil or criminal proceedings in any court of the\nCommonwealth, of a State or of a Territory:\n\n(a) a statement or disclosure made by the person at a private\nsession;\n\n(b) the production of a document or other thing by the person at\na private session.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply to the admissibility of evidence in\nproceedings for an offence against this Act.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:royal-commissions-amendment-act-2013-sch-1-sec-6oe-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:royal-commissions-amendment-act-2013-sch-1-sec-6oe-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f3f718f377e11f1548308676e39eca3fc814e502da3a0b52a619a25355ae2bf0"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/royal-commissions-amendment-act-2013#sch-1-sec-6oe",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "6OE Statements made and documents produced etc. at a private",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 14,
      "values:originalText": "session are not admissible in evidence\n\n(1) The following are not admissible in evidence against a natural\nperson in any civil or criminal proceedings in any court of the\nCommonwealth, of a State or of a Territory:\n\n(a) a statement or disclosure made by the person at a private\nsession;\n\n(b) the production of a document or other thing by the person at\na private session.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply to the admissibility of evidence in\nproceedings for an offence against this Act."
    },
