      "dc:source": "royal-commissions-amendment-act-2013.pdf, p.16",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A provision of a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory\nhas no effect to the extent that it would otherwise require or\nauthorise a person to make a record of, use or disclose information\nobtained at a private session if the record, use or disclosure:\n\n(a) would contravene a provision of this Division; or\n\n(b) would not be permitted by a provision of this Division.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) has effect whether the provision concerned is made\nbefore or after the commencement of this section.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A provision of a law of the Commonwealth, a State or a Territory\nhas no effect to the extent that it would otherwise require or\nauthorise a person to make a record of, use or disclose information\nobtained at a private session if the record, use or disclosure:\n\n(a) would contravene a provision of this Division; or\n\n(b) would not be permitted by a provision of this Division.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) has effect whether the provision concerned is made\nbefore or after the commencement of this section.",
